GIVEN row IS A `Cross-reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the cross-reference is to an indexed provision under its printed heading` MEANS
        `the provision is in the index` (row's `citing provision`)
    AND `the heading of the provision` (row's `cited identifier`) EQUALS JUST (row's `heading of the cited provision as printed`)

GIVEN row IS A `Reference to another instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference to another instrument is not resolved in the index` MEANS
        `the provision is in the index` (row's `citing provision`)
    AND (NOT `the provision is in the index` (row's `instrument as printed`))
